' The SyncPlay coordinator's decisions, pure: no node, no Timer, no HTTP. SyncPlayManager holds
' the clocks and the player, asks these functions what to do, and does it.
'
' Four concerns live here:
'   - scheduleCommand: when (on the device clock) a server command applies, and at what position.
'   - applyPlan: the transport verbs that carry a command out on the player, in order.
'   - the settle correction: how far this member sits from the group, and how it corrects that.
'   - the ready tracker: when to tell the server this member is Buffering, and when it is Ready.
'
' The rules follow jellyfin-web's PlaybackCore (read at v10.11.0, unchanged since 10.7.0) where
' the server's expectations make them the only correct ones, and depart from it where a device
' measurement says so: Ready after a seek waits for a position notification near the target,
' because at the `playing` edge the Video node can still read the pre-seek position (seen once
' in ten seeks across the two test devices, 2026-10-23), and the server corrects any Ready more
' than MaxPlaybackOffset (500 ms on every server line) off with a Seek command.
' Every time is a LongInteger: epoch milliseconds or Jellyfin ticks (decision
' syncplay-time-longinteger).
namespace syncPlayPlayback

  ' An Unpause seeks first only when the player is further off than this (web's minDelaySkipToSync).
  const SKIP_TO_SYNC_MIN_MS = 400
  ' A seek counts as landed once a position notification is within this of the target: the
  ' server's own tolerance on a Ready report (Group.MaxPlaybackOffset).
  const READY_TOLERANCE_MS = 500
  ' How long to wait for that notification before reporting Ready with the position in hand. The
  ' Stick 4K took up to 2.6 s from the seek write to `playing` on direct play (2026-10-23).
  const SEEK_SETTLE_MS = 3000
  ' A `buffering` that outlasts this is a stall worth reporting. The node passes through
  ' `buffering` for a few milliseconds on a pause and a resume (4 to 16 ms measured 2026-10-23), and
  ' reporting those made the server pause the whole group twice over per command.
  const STALL_MS = 1000
  ' How long after a pause write the manager checks that it took. A pause landed in under 10 ms
  ' in the phase A spike (2026-10-23) and by the first 200 ms sample on 2026-10-24, so this leaves
  ' headroom.
  const PAUSE_CONFIRM_MS = 1000
  ' The most pause writes the manager makes for one group command.
  const PAUSE_ATTEMPTS = 3
  ' After an Unpause, once the node plays, a member further ahead of the group than this holds
  ' (settleCorrectionDue). A hold costs a freeze as long as the drift, so it is worth doing small.
  ' A member behind has to seek, which froze the picture for 2.1 to 2.6 s (Stick 4K, 2026-10-31),
  ' so that side waits for SKIP_TO_SYNC_MIN_MS, the bar web sets for a skip.
  const SETTLE_CORRECTION_MS = 150
  ' Position notifications to let pass after `playing` before the drift is read: the node's
  ' position field lags real playback by up to one notification interval.
  const SETTLE_POSITIONS = 2
  ' How far ahead of the group a correction seeks before it pauses and waits for the group to
  ' arrive. A plain seek to the group's position lands behind by the seek's own latency (a
  ' transcode resumed 364 and 667 ms late on a 2026-10-31 Stick 4K run, the drift it was meant
  ' to fix), so the correction uses the protocol's own shape: seek past the group, pause there,
  ' resume when the group reaches it. A seek can take longer (a correction's outlasted this on
  ' direct play and left the member 1.9 s behind, Stick 4K, 2026-10-31), so the lead grows to
  ' what the last seek on this node took (correctionLeadMs). This is the shortest it gets.
  const CORRECTION_LEAD_MS = 2000
  ' What a lead keeps over the last seek's time, for a seek a little slower than the one before.
  const CORRECTION_LEAD_MARGIN_MS = 500

  ' --- scheduling ---

  ' When and how a parsed, accepted SyncPlayCommand applies.
  ' @param estimator - the syncPlayOffset estimator (hasEstimate must be true)
  ' @param command - a syncPlayMessage "syncplaycommand" AA
  ' @param nowMs - the device clock now
  ' @returns an AA with action, delayMs and positionTicks: delayMs is 0 when `When` has passed. An Unpause
  '   whose When has passed carries the position the group is at now, estimated forward from the
  '   command's own position (web's estimateCurrentTicks); every other command keeps its ticks.
  function scheduleCommand(estimator as object, command as object, nowMs as longinteger) as object
    applyAtMs& = syncPlayOffset.deviceTimeForServerMs(estimator, command.whenMs)
    delay& = applyAtMs& - nowMs
    if delay& < 0 then delay& = 0&
    positionTicks& = syncPlayTime.asLong(command.positionTicks)
    if command.command = "Unpause" and delay& = 0
      serverNow& = syncPlayOffset.serverNowMs(estimator, nowMs)
      positionTicks& = positionTicks& + syncPlayTime.msToTicks(serverNow& - command.whenMs)
    end if
    return { action: command.command, delayMs: delay&, positionTicks: positionTicks& }
  end function

  ' The transport verbs (PlayerHostView.handleTransport's evt shapes) that carry a plan out, in
  ' order. A seek step carries two flags for the ready tracker: `report` says the server waits on
  ' this seek (a Seek command: Buffering, then Ready once it lands), and `thenPause` says to pause
  ' once it lands, which is how a Seek leaves the player for the Unpause that follows (web's
  ' scheduleSeek). The seek inside an Unpause is a local correction the server already accounts
  ' for, so it is silent.
  '
  ' Three rules the Stick 4K taught. A `seek` on a paused Video node resumes it (2026-10-23), so a
  ' Pause only pauses (the next Unpause carries the position and corrects it), a Seek sends
  ' no `resume` of its own, and an Unpause that seeks sends no `resume` either. A `resume` (a
  ' control `play`) written to a node that is still buffering from a seek leaves it buffering for
  ' good (2026-10-23), and a buffering node plays by itself once it has buffered, so an Unpause
  ' sends `resume` only to a paused node. And a `pause` written to a buffering node lands `paused`
  ' at once and stays there (measured 2026-10-24, direct play, a seek to 150 s, two runs): the
  ' wedge of 2026-10-23 came from a `play` or `resume` written while buffering, so a Pause
  ' pauses a buffering node too. A load is the exception: its first-frame pause (the tracker's
  ' `pauseFirst`) owns that, and a pause during a load was never measured. A seek in flight is
  ' the other: a `pause` written there can leave the node buffering for good (the node can still
  ' read `playing` right after the seek write), so a Pause writes nothing and the seek's landing
  ' pauses instead, with the OSD up (the manager calls `pauseAfterSeek`).
  ' @param plan - from scheduleCommand
  ' @param playerState - the Video node's `state`
  ' @param playerPositionTicks - the player's last known position
  ' @param trackerPhase - the ready tracker's phase, to tell a load from a stall
  ' @param heldForCorrection - the node is paused for a drift correction, so a group Pause is news
  '   to the viewer though it needs no pause of its own
  function applyPlan(plan as object, playerState as string, playerPositionTicks as longinteger, trackerPhase = "" as string, heldForCorrection = false as boolean) as object
    steps = []
    target = { command: "seekto", position: ticksToSeconds(plan.positionTicks), report: false, thenPause: false }
    if plan.action = "Unpause"
      ' A load's first frame pauses and reports Ready, and the server answers that Ready with the
      ' group's position. A server from 12.1 stops waiting after 30 s and sends this before the
      ' first frame: a seek written here chased the load, and left a member 23 s behind on a slow
      ' file (Stick 4K, 2026-10-31).
      if trackerPhase = "loading" then return steps
      needsSeek = Abs(playerPositionTicks - plan.positionTicks) > syncPlayTime.msToTicks(SKIP_TO_SYNC_MIN_MS)
      if needsSeek then steps.push(target)
      if playerState = "paused" and not needsSeek then steps.push({ command: "resume" })
    else if plan.action = "Pause"
      if pauseWaitsForSeek(trackerPhase)
        ' The seek's landing pauses.
      else if playerState = "playing" or (playerState = "buffering" and trackerPhase <> "loading") or heldForCorrection
        steps.push({ command: "pause", showOsd: true })
      end if
    else if plan.action = "Seek"
      target.report = true
      target.thenPause = true
      steps.push(target)
    else if plan.action = "Stop"
      steps.push({ command: "stop" })
    end if
    return steps
  end function

  ' Whether a seek is in flight, so a Pause is left to the seek's landing (pauseAfterSeek) and
  ' writes nothing of its own, and a Seek waits for it (the tracker's "holdSeek").
  function pauseWaitsForSeek(trackerPhase as string) as boolean
    return trackerPhase = "seeking" or trackerPhase = "landing"
  end function

  ' Whether the player owes the group a pause: the group is paused and the node plays on. The
  ' load and seek phases pause by themselves (pauseFirst, thenPause), so only a settled phase
  ' counts.
  function owesPause(groupPaused as boolean, playerState as string, trackerPhase as string) as boolean
    if not groupPaused then return false
    if trackerPhase <> "ready" and trackerPhase <> "stalling" and trackerPhase <> "rebuffering" then return false
    return playerState = "playing" or playerState = "buffering"
  end function

  ' Where a new playlist starts for this member: the last Unpause estimated forward when it is
  ' newer than the queue update (web's startPlayback), a newer Pause or Seek's own position (the
  ' group stands there; a halted member resuming into a paused group lands where it waits), else
  ' the update's own start. Web estimates forward from the update's LastUpdate even for a paused
  ' group and then takes the corrective Seek; the update's position as is reports the paused
  ' player where it is.
  function startPositionTicks(update as object, lastCommand as dynamic, estimator as object, nowMs as longinteger) as longinteger
    if isValid(lastCommand) and lastCommand.emittedAtMs >= update.lastUpdateMs
      if lastCommand.command = "Unpause"
        serverNow& = syncPlayOffset.serverNowMs(estimator, nowMs)
        return syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.positionTicks) + syncPlayTime.msToTicks(serverNow& - lastCommand.whenMs)
      end if
      if lastCommand.command = "Pause" or lastCommand.command = "Seek" then return syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.positionTicks)
    end if
    return syncPlayTime.asLong(update.startPositionTicks)
  end function

  ' --- the settle correction ---

  ' The command that says where the group is now, or invalid when none does. A new item's load runs
  ' under the last item's Unpause, so only a command for the playing item counts. A Buffering this
  ' member reported ends it too: the group waits for this member, and a server from 12.1 answers
  ' its recovery with an Unpause to the others alone, so the last Unpause would run on through a
  ' wait this member never hears of. The next command it schedules says where the group is again.
  function clockReference(lastCommand as dynamic, playingItemId as string, reportedBuffering as boolean) as dynamic
    if reportedBuffering or not isValid(lastCommand) or lastCommand.playlistItemId <> playingItemId then return invalid
    return lastCommand
  end function

  ' How far this member sits from the group, in ms, positive when it is behind: the last
  ' Unpause's position run forward on the measured clock, minus the player's position (web's
  ' playbackDiffMillis). Invalid while no Unpause is in force or its When has not come.
  function driftMs(lastCommand as dynamic, estimator as object, nowMs as longinteger, playerPositionTicks as longinteger) as dynamic
    if not isValid(lastCommand) or lastCommand.command <> "Unpause" then return invalid
    serverNow& = syncPlayOffset.serverNowMs(estimator, nowMs)
    whenMs& = syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.whenMs)
    if serverNow& < whenMs& then return invalid
    estimated& = syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.positionTicks)) + (serverNow& - whenMs&)
    return estimated& - syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(playerPositionTicks)
  end function

  ' The check an Unpause arms: once the node plays and SETTLE_POSITIONS notifications have come,
  ' a drift past its threshold is corrected, and then the check is spent until the next
  ' Unpause. A correction gets one reading after it (retrySettleCheck), so the most an Unpause can
  ' cost is two.
  function newSettleCheck() as object
    return { armed: false, positions: 0, retried: false }
  end function

  sub armSettleCheck(check as object)
    check.armed = true
    check.positions = 0
    check.retried = false
  end sub

  ' A load starts over: the Unpause that armed this was for the item before it.
  sub disarmSettleCheck(check as object)
    check.armed = false
    check.positions = 0
  end sub

  ' A correction ended, well or badly: read the drift once more. A correction can land off (late,
  ' or at the wrong spot on a transcode), and nothing else would look again before the next
  ' Unpause. Once per arming, so a node that never lands cannot seek for good.
  sub retrySettleCheck(check as object)
    if check.retried then return
    check.retried = true
    check.armed = true
    check.positions = 0
  end sub

  ' Feed one position notification. True when a correction is due now (correctionPlan says
  ' where to seek and when to resume): past SETTLE_CORRECTION_MS ahead of the group, past
  ' SKIP_TO_SYNC_MIN_MS behind it. Nothing is counted while the group is paused, the node is not playing, or the tracker is not settled: the drift means
  ' nothing there, and web gates its correction on the same three. An unknown drift counts for
  ' nothing either, so a reading that comes too early cannot spend the check.
  function settleCorrectionDue(check as object, drift as dynamic, playerState as string, trackerPhase as string, groupPaused as boolean) as boolean
    if not check.armed then return false
    if groupPaused or playerState <> "playing" or trackerPhase <> "ready" then return false
    if not isValid(drift) then return false
    check.positions++
    if check.positions < SETTLE_POSITIONS then return false
    check.armed = false
    if drift >= 0 then return drift > SKIP_TO_SYNC_MIN_MS
    return Abs(drift) > SETTLE_CORRECTION_MS
  end function

  ' The correction for a drift the check found. Behind the group: seek to the group's position
  ' plus the lead and pause once the node is there (the tracker's thenPause). Ahead of it: pause
  ' where it is, since waiting needs no seek and so no jump or rebuffer. Either way the node
  ' resumes on the device clock at the moment the group's own clock reaches that position.
  ' @param drift - from driftMs
  ' @param playerPositionTicks - the player's position the drift was read against
  ' @param lastCommand - the Unpause in force
  ' @param leadMs - how far past the group a seek goes (correctionLeadMs)
  ' @returns an AA with seek, targetTicks and resumeAtMs, the resume moment on the device clock
  function correctionPlan(drift as longinteger, playerPositionTicks as longinteger, lastCommand as object, estimator as object, leadMs as longinteger) as object
    seek = drift >= 0
    targetTicks& = playerPositionTicks
    if seek then targetTicks& = playerPositionTicks + syncPlayTime.msToTicks(drift) + syncPlayTime.msToTicks(leadMs)
    commandMs& = syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.positionTicks))
    reachesServerMs& = syncPlayTime.asLong(lastCommand.whenMs) + (syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(targetTicks&) - commandMs&)
    return { seek: seek, targetTicks: targetTicks&, resumeAtMs: syncPlayOffset.deviceTimeForServerMs(estimator, reachesServerMs&) }
  end function

  ' How far past the group a correction's seek goes: long enough to land before the group arrives,
  ' judged by the last seek on this node. A seek too slow for any lead becomes a stall the server
  ' hears of (trackPlayerEvent), so it never reaches this.
  ' @param lastSeekMs - how long the last seek took; 0 while none has landed on this player
  function correctionLeadMs(lastSeekMs as longinteger) as longinteger
    leadMs& = lastSeekMs + CORRECTION_LEAD_MARGIN_MS
    if leadMs& < CORRECTION_LEAD_MS then return CORRECTION_LEAD_MS
    return leadMs&
  end function

  ' Move the resume to where the node stopped: a seek lands off its target (up to 36 ms in the logs
  ' of a 2026-10-31 Stick 4K run), and resuming on the target's moment carries that error into the
  ' group. A paused position further off than the landing tolerance is not one to trust, so the
  ' plan's own moment stands. Safe to call again: the plan then holds the position it moved to.
  sub landCorrection(plan as object, pausedTicks as longinteger)
    if Abs(pausedTicks - plan.targetTicks) > syncPlayTime.msToTicks(READY_TOLERANCE_MS) then return
    plan.resumeAtMs = plan.resumeAtMs + syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(pausedTicks - plan.targetTicks)
    plan.targetTicks = pausedTicks
  end sub

  ' Whether a seek would run off the item. The player turns a target at or past the end into a seek
  ' 30 s short of it (voiceTransport.computeSeekStatus), so the correction skips it; the item is
  ' about to end anyway.
  ' @param durationSeconds - the player's effective duration; 0 or invalid while unknown
  function seekPastEnd(targetTicks as longinteger, durationSeconds as dynamic) as boolean
    if not isValid(durationSeconds) or durationSeconds <= 0 then return false
    return ticksToSeconds(targetTicks) >= durationSeconds
  end function

  ' Milliseconds until the correction's resume, 0 when the moment has passed (a seek slower than
  ' the lead: the resume goes out as the node pauses, and the check reads the drift again).
  function correctionResumeDelayMs(plan as object, nowMs as longinteger) as longinteger
    delay& = syncPlayTime.asLong(plan.resumeAtMs) - nowMs
    if delay& < 0 then return 0&
    return delay&
  end function

  ' --- the ready tracker ---

  ' Phases: "idle" (no player, or nothing owed), "loading" (a player mounted, no first frame yet),
  ' "seeking" (a seek is out, waiting for a position near the target), "landing" (the position
  ' is there but the node is still buffering: the seek's pause and the Ready wait for `playing`,
  ' which confirms the position before the pause),
  ' "ready" (the server has this member's position), "stalling" (buffering after ready, not yet
  ' long enough to report), "rebuffering" (a stall the server was told about).
  '
  ' `heldSeek` is a seek that came in while another was in flight ({ targetTicks, report,
  ' thenPause }, or invalid). The node never runs two seeks at once, because two overlapping
  ' ones can leave it buffering for good: the newest wins, and it goes out as the seek in flight
  ' ends (the result's `nextSeek`).
  function newReadyTracker() as object
    return { phase: "idle", targetTicks: 0&, lastPositionTicks: 0&, lastState: "", reportSeek: false, thenPause: false, showOsd: false, loadStartTicks: 0&, heldSeek: invalid }
  end function

  ' Feed one player or coordinator event; get back what to send and what to wait for.
  ' @param tracker - from newReadyTracker, mutated in place
  ' @param evt - { kind: "mounted" | "seek" | "holdSeek" | "state" | "position" | "timeout" | "unmounted",
  '   state (for "state"), positionTicks (for "seek", "state" and "position"), for "mounted" the
  '   `startTicks` the load was asked to start at (absent when it starts at the beginning), and for
  '   "seek" the plan step's `report` and `thenPause` }. A silent seek (report false) still enters
  '   the seeking phase, so the buffering and playing it causes are not taken for a stall.
  '   "holdSeek" carries `targetTicks` (not `positionTicks`, which every event copies into the
  '   tracker's last position), `report` and `thenPause`: a seek due while one is in flight.
  ' @returns an AA with report ("", "buffering" or "ready"), waitMs, pauseFirst, showOsd, nextSeek and
  '   positionTicks:
  '   `waitMs` above 0 asks for a one-shot timer that feeds back { kind: "timeout" }; `pauseFirst`
  '   says to pause the player before the Ready goes out (a load's first frame: web pauses at
  '   playbackstart and reports Ready, and the server's Unpause then starts everyone together);
  '   `showOsd` says that pause is a group Pause that waited for the seek (pauseAfterSeek), so
  '   it shows the OSD as the Play key does;
  '   `nextSeek` is the held seek ({ targetTicks, report, thenPause }) to write now that the one in
  '   flight is over, or invalid. The phase stays "seeking" and nothing else is reported, so the
  '   caller writes it and feeds it back as a "seek" event;
  '   `positionTicks` is the position to put in the report, or -1 to use the player's own. A load
  '   that started partway in has a Video node still reading 0 at its first `playing` (a probe on
  '   2026-10-23 read 0.0 while buffering and 349.0 right after), and a Ready at 0 makes the server
  '   send a corrective Seek, so that first Ready carries the start instead.
  function trackPlayerEvent(tracker as object, evt as object) as object
    result = { report: "", waitMs: 0, pauseFirst: false, showOsd: false, positionTicks: -1&, nextSeek: invalid }
    if not isValid(evt) or not syncPlayTime.isText(evt.kind) then return result
    kind = evt.kind
    if syncPlayTime.isWholeNumber(evt.positionTicks) then tracker.lastPositionTicks = syncPlayTime.asLong(evt.positionTicks)

    if kind = "mounted"
      tracker.phase = "loading"
      tracker.heldSeek = invalid
      tracker.loadStartTicks = 0&
      if syncPlayTime.isWholeNumber(evt.startTicks) then tracker.loadStartTicks = syncPlayTime.asLong(evt.startTicks)
      result.report = "buffering"
    else if kind = "seek"
      tracker.phase = "seeking"
      tracker.targetTicks = syncPlayTime.asLong(evt.positionTicks)
      tracker.reportSeek = evt.report = true
      tracker.thenPause = evt.thenPause = true
      ' The node's position can reach the target before it reports buffering, so the state
      ' from before the seek says nothing: forget it and wait for the node's next state.
      tracker.lastState = ""
      if tracker.reportSeek then result.report = "buffering"
      result.waitMs = SEEK_SETTLE_MS
    else if kind = "holdSeek"
      held = { targetTicks: syncPlayTime.asLong(evt.targetTicks), report: evt.report = true, thenPause: evt.thenPause = true }
      if Abs(held.targetTicks - tracker.targetTicks) <= syncPlayTime.msToTicks(READY_TOLERANCE_MS)
        ' The seek in flight already goes there: it takes on what this one asked for.
        tracker.reportSeek = tracker.reportSeek or held.report
        tracker.thenPause = held.thenPause
        tracker.heldSeek = invalid
      else
        tracker.heldSeek = held
      end if
    else if kind = "state"
      state = ""
      if syncPlayTime.isText(evt.state) then state = evt.state
      tracker.lastState = state
      if tracker.phase = "landing"
        if state = "playing" or state = "paused" then seekSettled(tracker, result, state = "playing")
      else if state = "playing" and tracker.phase = "loading"
        tracker.phase = "ready"
        result.report = "ready"
        result.pauseFirst = true
        if tracker.loadStartTicks - tracker.lastPositionTicks > syncPlayTime.msToTicks(READY_TOLERANCE_MS) then result.positionTicks = tracker.loadStartTicks
      else if state = "buffering" and tracker.phase = "ready"
        tracker.phase = "stalling"
        result.waitMs = STALL_MS
      else if (state = "playing" or state = "paused") and tracker.phase = "stalling"
        tracker.phase = "ready"
      else if state = "playing" and tracker.phase = "rebuffering"
        tracker.phase = "ready"
        result.report = "ready"
      end if
    else if kind = "position"
      if tracker.phase = "seeking" and Abs(tracker.lastPositionTicks - tracker.targetTicks) <= syncPlayTime.msToTicks(READY_TOLERANCE_MS)
        seekLanded(tracker, result)
      end if
    else if kind = "timeout"
      if tracker.phase = "seeking"
        seekLanded(tracker, result)
      else if tracker.phase = "landing"
        if releaseHeldSeek(tracker, result) then return result
        if tracker.lastState = "buffering" and not tracker.reportSeek
          ' A silent seek this slow is a stall: the group waits, as for any other, rather than
          ' play on while this member falls behind in silence. The Ready that ends it goes out at
          ' the next `playing`, and any Pause by then is the group's own (owesPause).
          tracker.phase = "rebuffering"
          tracker.thenPause = false
          tracker.showOsd = false
          result.report = "buffering"
        else
          ' The node never reached playing: report what there is, and pause nothing.
          seekSettled(tracker, result, false)
        end if
      else if tracker.phase = "stalling"
        tracker.phase = "rebuffering"
        result.report = "buffering"
      end if
    else if kind = "unmounted"
      tracker.phase = "idle"
      tracker.heldSeek = invalid
    end if
    return result
  end function

  ' The seek's position is there, which the node can report before it reports `buffering`, so
  ' every seek waits (the landing phase) for the node's state: `playing` confirms the position
  ' before any pause, and `paused` needs no pause. Settling here would take the buffering still to
  ' come for a stall, and a stall report pauses the whole group.
  sub seekLanded(tracker as object, result as object)
    if tracker.lastState <> "playing" and tracker.lastState <> "paused"
      tracker.phase = "landing"
      result.waitMs = SEEK_SETTLE_MS
      return
    end if
    seekSettled(tracker, result, tracker.lastState = "playing")
  end sub

  ' The pause a seek's landing owes no longer stands: a correction was given up, or an Unpause came
  ' first. Nothing would resume the node if it paused.
  sub abandonSeekPause(tracker as object)
    tracker.thenPause = false
    tracker.showOsd = false
  end sub

  ' The seek in flight is over and a newer one was held: it goes next, in its place. The phase stays
  ' "seeking", with no report, pause or Ready, so the group sees one seek that ends where the newest does.
  ' @returns true when a held seek was released into result.nextSeek
  function releaseHeldSeek(tracker as object, result as object) as boolean
    if not isValid(tracker.heldSeek) then return false
    result.nextSeek = tracker.heldSeek
    tracker.heldSeek = invalid
    tracker.phase = "seeking"
    return true
  end function

  ' A held seek no longer stands: an Unpause says where the group is now.
  sub dropHeldSeek(tracker as object)
    tracker.heldSeek = invalid
  end sub

  ' A group Pause came in while a seek was in flight: the seek's landing pauses the node, with
  ' the OSD up, in place of a pause written to a node that is still seeking.
  sub pauseAfterSeek(tracker as object)
    tracker.thenPause = true
    tracker.showOsd = true
  end sub

  ' Ready again: reported, and preceded by a pause, when the step asked for them.
  sub seekSettled(tracker as object, result as object, pauseNow as boolean)
    if releaseHeldSeek(tracker, result) then return
    tracker.phase = "ready"
    if tracker.reportSeek then result.report = "ready"
    result.pauseFirst = tracker.thenPause and pauseNow
    result.showOsd = tracker.showOsd
    tracker.reportSeek = false
    tracker.thenPause = false
    tracker.showOsd = false
  end sub

  ' Whether a seek that was in flight is over, the tracker having moved from `before` to `now`.
  function seekEnded(before as string, now as string) as boolean
    return pauseWaitsForSeek(before) and (now = "ready" or now = "rebuffering")
  end function

  ' Whether the viewer should take this member as paused, which the node's state alone does not say.
  ' A drift correction's hold is not the viewer's pause, and a pause waiting on a seek's landing is
  ' theirs though the node still plays. Their controls ask this, so a press means what they see.
  ' @param nodeState - the Video node's `state`
  ' @param correcting - a drift correction is under way
  ' @param pauseWaiting - a pause waits on a seek's landing (the tracker's `showOsd`)
  function pausedForViewer(nodeState as string, correcting as boolean, pauseWaiting as boolean) as boolean
    if pauseWaiting then return true
    if correcting then return false
    return nodeState = "paused"
  end function

  ' --- units ---

  ' The Video node's `position` and `seek` are float seconds; the wire is ticks.
  function secondsToTicks(seconds as dynamic) as longinteger
    if not isValid(seconds) then return 0&
    ms& = Int(seconds * 1000)
    return syncPlayTime.msToTicks(ms&)
  end function

  function ticksToSeconds(ticks as longinteger) as float
    return syncPlayTime.ticksToMs(ticks) / 1000#
  end function

end namespace
